{
  "source": {
    "what": "The spell scaling the game shows for a staff or a seal, where it shows an attack rating for every other armament: 28 catalysts x 3 Nightfarers, no relics, each catalyst at its own rarity.",
    "sheet": "Nightreign Weapon Scaling.xlsx, sheet \"Weapon Attack Power\", rows 294-321, columns Duchess / Revenant / Recluse -- supplied by the App Designer",
    "read_on": "2026-09-05",
    "game_data_version": "10350000",
    "measured_by": "docs/berichte/T-043-qa-engineer.md (T-043), QA-099. The 84 cells here were read out of the sheet again for this file rather than copied from that report; they agree with the three examples the report prints (Carian Regal Scepter 218/198/237, Recluse's Staff 118/107/128, Frenzied Flame Seal 172/212/212).",
    "levels": "Level 12 for all three columns. The attributes are not written into this file: the test computes them with model.compute, which gives Duchess INT 36 / FAI 24, Revenant INT 27 / FAI 45, Recluse INT 45 / FAI 45 -- the values T-043 measured against.",
    "left_out": [
      "The Wylder, Guardian, Ironeye, Raider and Executor columns: the sheet leaves the catalyst block empty for them.",
      "Upgraded catalysts: the sheet reads each armament at its own rarity, so nothing here says what a reinforced staff shows.",
      "The 227 unnamed catalyst rows of the params: same structure, no figure to compare against.",
      "What a spell actually hits for: this is the scaling the game displays, and MagicParam was never read."
    ],
    "how_these_rows_were_picked": "Every catalyst row of the sheet, all 28, and every column that carries figures for them, all 3. Nothing was selected: the block is contiguous (rows 294-321) and it is taken whole.",
    "not_a_selection_of_the_hits": "floor(90 x reinforce.catalyst_scaling x (1 + curve16(INT or FAI)/100)) reproduces 84 of 84 of these cells exactly, with no exception and nothing left out. Verified 2026-09-05 for T-046, and by T-043 before it on the same sheet.",
    "name_collisions": "Two of the sheet's names belong to two rows each in the data. `Recluse Staff` is 33750000, the Recluse's own starting armament: the other row, 33770000, holds no spell (equippedSpell_R1/R2 = -1), sits on the generic reinforce group 0 and would read 151 where the sheet reads 128. `Finger Seal` is taken as 34750000; the other row, 34000000, sits on the same reinforce group 6000 and is figure-for-figure identical, so that pairing cannot be wrong in a way this file could show (QA-099 a, QA-099 b)."
  },
